.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt BUS_ID_MATCH 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm bus_id_match
.Nd match device against a generic ID entry
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/kern/bus.h
.In sys/kern/driver.h
.Ft int
.Fn bus_id_match "const struct device_id *id" "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn bus_id_match
function determines if a device matches a specific ID criteria. It checks the
device's vendor ID, device ID, and class code against the provided
.Fa id
structure.
.Pp
The matching rules are:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Va vendor_id :
Must match
.Va dev->vendor_id
unless set to
.Dv DEVICE_ID_ANY .
.It
.Va device_id :
Must match
.Va dev->device_id
unless set to
.Dv DEVICE_ID_ANY .
.It
.Va class_id / class_mask :
The device's class is constructed as
.Pq "class << 16 | subclass << 8 | progif" .
The masked value must match
.Va id->class_id .
If
.Va class_mask
is 0, the class check is skipped.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 1 if the device matches the ID entry, 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr driver 9 ,
.Xr device 9
